[size=5]Description[/size]
Compact Inventory makes every item take one cell (1x1) in the character bag and storage grids. A large item such as Whole Lamb or Rack of Ribs takes the same space as a small item, so you manage inventory by item count and weight instead of shape.

[size=5]Main features[/size]
[list]
[*][b]Existing saves included.[/b] Items already in a save become 1x1 when you load it with the mod installed.[/*]
[*][b]Other inventory limits stay the same.[/b] The mod does not change item weight, stack limits, or bag sizes.[/*]
[/list]

[size=5]Requirements[/size]
[list]
[*][url=https://www.nexusmods.com/survivallog/mods/12]BepInEx for Survival Log[/url]. Install it first.[/*]
[/list]

[size=5]Installation[/size]
[list=1]
[*]Install [url=https://www.nexusmods.com/survivallog/mods/12]BepInEx[/url] [i](if no other mods were installed before, start the game once so BepInEx finishes setup, then quit)[/i].[/*]
[*]Extract this mod's zip into the game folder (the folder with the game .exe). The DLL lands in BepInEx\plugins. Full path example:
[code]C:\Program Files (x86)\Steam\steamapps\common\Survival Log\BepInEx\plugins\CompactInventory.dll[/code]
[/*]
[/list]

[size=5]Uninstall[/size]
Delete [font=Courier New]CompactInventory.dll[/font] from the [font=Courier New]BepInEx\plugins[/font] folder.

Before uninstalling, back up your save and spread out or remove items from crowded bags, then save. Items regain their normal size on the next load. The game may rearrange items or drop some beside storage. Check the ground afterward. Making room may help, but is not guaranteed to prevent this.

